+# V4 closed native comparison: coupling without sampled behavioral change
+
+## Frozen source and allocation
+
+Source commit fb918e29a612be0cef6d2a0e5885f04d7f0b7d1f, tree 2854ee759e9d0fe6a018738db72e6e8a8b359018. Candidate source was already frozen at 7a33245ff19e2cb6cf592a8d8728eced55956540. The predeclared plan completed exactly 512 ordinary CPU world intervals: four factors × peer/toy × loneliness 0/.15 × 32. Every interval yielded a decision, with three neural microsteps. Constructor/biology/world equality, exact final native encoder reconstruction, and unchanged founder optimizer checks all passed. Lifetime plasticity was enabled.
+
+The unchanged factor is the explicit SignedChoiceReadouts research recipe, NOT the unconfigured app default genome. No accepted creature, loaded state or default asset was changed. No source/weight/exposure extension followed the outcomes.
+
+Raw local receipt SHA256 fb17d4960ff9f11e77e947061ebc948bf143da68bfa875f41f1724e178c2b77c. It contains complete disposable replay arrays and must remain local. The accompanying scalar summary excludes those arrays.
+
+## Actual acted results
+
+All 24 pairwise factor/context comparisons have zero differences in their 32 representative/motor candidate choices. Different log probabilities are not counted as different actions. This is a closed result of no sampled behavioral change, not a successful social preference or learning advantage.
+
+The direct source now produces a measurable new-port contribution. At initial loneliness .15, the largest contribution is .000553131 for toy and .000492573 for peer. Corresponding constant-reference maxima are .000248432 and .000247478. At zero need, direct and constant agree. The largest contribution/global candidate top-gap ratio is .001737914 (0.174%); this is not a conditional factorized-channel gap. Temperature is 1, so the maximum contribution/temperature is .000553131. These small scales are consistent with the absence of changed sampled choices, but do not prove a larger coefficient would improve behavior.
+
+Each .15 context contains 57 positive, 51 negative and 276 zero recalled family-value samples. Zero-need contexts have 108 negative and 276 zero. These are acquired aggregate family valences, not isolated social-need relief labels. Ordinary peer contact reduces final loneliness to 0 versus .0406228602 for toy, identically across factors. That verifies world relief, not a learned preference for peers.
+
+The zero-initial readout develops effective lifetime offsets up to 3.72267e-6. Its same-state effective-head ablation remains zero at the recorded f32 logit precision. It is therefore wrong to call that lived control permanently disconnected. The active direct maximum effective offset is 3.69866e-6; initial genetic weights remain .35. Full per-context maxima are recorded in the safe summary.
+
+## Exact same-state counterfactuals
+
+Final replay context, acquired offsets, actual recall, other inputs and native receptor effects are held fixed. At 32 frames/96 microsteps in the toy/.15 context, pressure 0/.05/.15 gives source .024399806/.036175545/.058955751. Direct new-port absolute maxima are .000247478/.000366926/.000597954. The constant control remains .000247478 at all three pressures. Pressure .8 gives .00190258, but was detached only and never acted in this allocation. Peer results are similar. Negative and positive acquired recalled values retain their corresponding contribution signs. Clearing lane32 produces exactly zero new-port contribution in every detached test.
+
+These are input counterfactuals, not alternate lives or recalculated memory query results. The raw receipt retains each row's contribution and global learned-offset extrema but not each row's final neural activation bank; only the final actual replay context is retained. Exact per-row source extrema cannot honestly be reconstructed from this file. The native tanh source is bounded within [-1,1], so the rectifier is [0,1]; the measured fixed receptor/fresh-state zero-to-one equilibrium range is approximately [.0244,.2220], not a universal bound over arbitrary metabolic/history states. The earlier elevated-metabolism test shows temporary gate closure is possible.
+
+## Finite follow-up proposal, not launched
+
+The route is no longer missing at its tested operating point. The remaining issue is useful scale and need specificity, not proof of a disconnected input. Keep V4 closed and unchanged.
+
+A separate explicitly identified coefficient candidate could compare gains 1 and 2 in detached replay only before considering any more acted intervals. Gain 2 is bounded analytically: under the qualified natural receptor context, the full-pressure source is approximately .222, so unit recalled valence contributes at most .444 before the existing shared memory clamp .5. It does not require a binary huge gain or changing the clamp. Gain 1 supplies an intermediate calibration point. Relative to .35, linear unsaturated projections of this allocation's largest contribution are only .00158 and .00316, still small versus typical competing logits. Those are projections, not executed results, and saturation/old-memory interactions must be measured.
+
+Freeze source identity and contrasts before any test: unchanged research recipe, zero-initial, constant-reference and direct factors; preserve both biases, all64 branches, ordinary plasticity and old rows. Test actual positive/negative/empty recorded recall and synthetic boundary values at pressures0/.05/.15/1, horizons1/8/32, plus elevated metabolic state. Require signed adverse outcomes to become less attractive, empty recall to add zero, exact same-state effective-head ablation, derivative/clamp/restore guards, and no forced action. Record all candidate/conditional logit gaps and final source activation scalars. No additional world exposure is authorized by this proposal itself; a finite acted plan must be frozen separately after review of those results.
+
+Even a stronger aggregate reader cannot distinguish which need an action relieved. Per-need family-conditioned consequence storage would require a separate versioned interface, not reinterpretation of old memory coordinates. No coefficient is claimed to repair all biological motivations.
+
+## Conditional channel audit from retained exact masks
+
+The stored action.motor_masks are the actual sampler masks; no candidate reconstruction or new replay is needed. Only Locomotion has multiple eligible enabled candidates. Each context has32 such rows,18 independently sampled and14 forced by the representative. In the direct/.15 toy context, conditional top-gap minimum is .007940769 and mean .3243718. The new head's change in the top pair's margin is at most1.525879e-5 absolute, with same-row ratio at most .00186153 (0.186%). Peer/.15 has gap minimum .00800705, mean .3242798, margin change at most3.242493e-5 and ratio .00393044 (0.393%). Zero-need differential effects are at f32 rounding scale. Much of the contribution is common within this channel. Raising a shared aggregate coefficient cannot by itself repair missing target/need distinction. The safe scalar summary records all factors, gaps, margin effects and forced counts.
